{"flags":["GST 2.0 effective date: sources (TOI, gaadikey, ETAuto) say 22 Sep 2025; task brief said 22 Sep 2026. Used 2025-09-22 throughout.","Honda Elevate original launch (4 Sep 2023, Rs 11L) precedes the window start (2023-10-01); excluded from launches.","No launch events found in window for city (5th-gen facelift was Mar 2023, out of window) or city-ehev (launched 2022, facelift Mar 2023, both out of window).","City Sport Edition (limited special edition, launched ~20 Jun 2025 at Rs 14.88-14.89L) and City Apex Edition / Elevate Black Edition / ADV Edition are special editions per rules, excluded from launches; Sports CVT GST price recorded with unmatched variant name.","Unresolved gap: pre-facelift Elevate prices (GaadiFy, Oct 2026) exceed Jan 2026 prices by ~Rs 17,000-21,000, suggesting an unsourced mid-2026 hike; not recorded as a price change (no date/source).","Verified variant-name mismatches: news trims 'VX' (City 2024-25), 'ZX Black'/'ZX Dual Tone' (Elevate) and 'Sports CVT' (City) have no exact match in verifiedData; recorded with closest names.","City e:HEV conflict: Autocar Jan 2025 figure (Rs 20,75,100) contradicts the May 2025 hike to Rs 20,85,000 implied by FE and the July 2025 cut baseline (Rs 20.85L); both recorded, treat with caution.","CarDekho Elevate CVT hike table (e.g. V R 13,71,000 -> 13,91,000) appears to describe the Jan 2025 hike, not a separate event; not used as an independent price change.","Current verified City line-up (ZX/ZX+ trims, SV at Rs 11,99,900) differs from the Sept 2025 GST price list (VX/ZX trims, SV at Rs 11,95,300), suggesting a post-GST City revision or new ZX+ top variant not researched in this pass; needs follow-up.","News 'ZX CVT' (City top trim in 2025) mapped to verified 'ZX 1.5P CVT', though verified data also lists 'ZX+ 1.5P CVT' as the current top trim; mapping is ambiguous.","Out of scope but notable: ET (Sept 2026) reports strong response to 'the new City and the ZR-V', indicating Honda ZR-V launched in India in 2026; flagged for the coordinator as a possible Honda launch event outside my model list."],"launches":[{"is_estimate":true,"launch_date":"2026-10-06","launch_price_inr":1180000,"launch_type":"Major facelift","model_id":"elevate","notes":"2026 Elevate facelift: pre-bookings opened 2026-10-01, launched 2026-10-06. Entry SV price unchanged at Rs 11.80L ex-showroom Delhi; new ZX+ top trim added (16.80/18.30L MT/CVT, Black 16.90/18.40L). Segment-first ventilated rear seats, 360-degree camera, connected LED lighting; 1.5L petrol unchanged. Full range 11.80-18.40L.","source_url":"https://www.carwale.com/news/2026-honda-elevate-launched-colours-and-variants-detailed/"}],"maker_id":"honda","model_notes":[{"model_id":"elevate","note":"Honda passed full GST 2.0 benefits on Elevate effective 22 Sep 2025 (Delhi ex-showroom): cuts of Rs 42,800-91,100 across variants; SV 11,91,000 -> 10,99,900 and top ZX CVT Dual Tone 16,93,000 -> 16,34,600. Honda stated strategic pricing valid till Dec 2025."},{"model_id":"elevate","note":"Pre-facelift Sept 2026 prices per GaadiFy comparison (SV 11.80L, V 12.27L, V CVT 13.43L, VX 13.92L, VX CVT 15.08L, ZX 15.18L, ZX CVT 16.36L) sit ~Rs 17,000-21,000 above Jan 2026 prices, implying an undocumented mid-2026 hike that could not be dated; not recorded as a price change."},{"model_id":"city","note":"Honda passed full GST 2.0 benefits on City effective 22 Sep 2025 (Delhi ex-showroom): cuts of Rs 42,700-57,500; SV 12,38,000 -> 11,95,300 and ZX CVT 16,64,900 -> 16,07,400, plus Sports CVT 14,88,900 -> 14,37,500. Strategic pricing valid till Dec 2025."},{"model_id":"city-ehev","note":"e:HEV line-up simplified to a single top-spec ZX trim in July 2025 (V discontinued) with a Rs 95,010 cut to Rs 19.89L; GST 2.0 then cut a further Rs 41,790 to Rs 19,48,200 w.e.f 22 Sep 2025."}],"price_changes":[{"effective_date":"2024-01-01","ex_showroom_price_inr":1157900,"is_estimate":true,"model_id":"elevate","notes":"Jan 2024 hike (reported early Jan 2024, ~4 months